# Line endings are repository policy, not per-developer configuration.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is a local git setting: it does not travel with a clone, so
# without this file every working tree diverged by platform. Two things broke
# as a result, both found on 2026-08-27:
#
#   1. Shell scripts checked out with CRLF, making the shebang `#!/bin/bash\r`,
#      which fails on Unix with `bad interpreter: ^M`. This affected
#      `.githooks/pre-commit` and the `plugins/prp-core/hooks/*.sh` scripts.
#   2. Content-invariant tests that slice source on a literal "\n" silently
#      changed meaning. `relay-field-findings-2026-08.test.mjs` sliced with
#      indexOf('\n}\n'), which returns -1 on a CRLF checkout, collapsing the
#      sliced function body to a 2-character string — so the test passed on
#      CI (LF) and failed on Windows (CRLF) against a correct implementation.
#
# The blobs in this repository are already stored with LF, so declaring the
# policy here changes no committed content; it only makes every checkout
# deterministic. Enforced mechanically by the `line-endings` check in
# `npm run validate`.

* text=auto eol=lf

# The single tracked binary.
*.docx binary
